{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01214",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.21,
      "end_seconds": 8.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.52,
      "end_seconds": 16.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 18.69,
      "end_seconds": 23.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Um, doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.52,
      "end_seconds": 30.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, I've been dealing with numbness in my feet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.11,
      "end_seconds": 32.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.07,
      "end_seconds": 35.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Probably three weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.89,
      "end_seconds": 45.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.84,
      "end_seconds": 63.36,
      "duration_seconds": 17.52,
      "text": "I'd say a couple of times a week. I'd give it a three, out of ten. Being unsteady in the dark was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.4,
      "end_seconds": 67.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.71,
      "end_seconds": 82.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.58,
      "end_seconds": 105.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.4, pressure 124 over 80, pulse is 73 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.66,
      "end_seconds": 108.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.48,
      "end_seconds": 114.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Right, they help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.17,
      "end_seconds": 120.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.32,
      "end_seconds": 133.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.61,
      "end_seconds": 138.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.17,
      "end_seconds": 161.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "The ankle reflexes are reduced and the feeling is dulled below the knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.37,
      "end_seconds": 164.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.14,
      "end_seconds": 176.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Have you had any bladder problems, back pain or weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.9,
      "end_seconds": 182.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "So, you know, no, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.32,
      "end_seconds": 187.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.86,
      "end_seconds": 190.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.35,
      "end_seconds": 193.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.92,
      "end_seconds": 197.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.6,
      "end_seconds": 202.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.98,
      "end_seconds": 214.01,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "Yes, I had my womb taken out, fifteen years ago. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.21,
      "end_seconds": 219.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.37,
      "end_seconds": 226.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Milk. I come out in... well, a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.28,
      "end_seconds": 238.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.04,
      "end_seconds": 244.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.97,
      "end_seconds": 248.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.49,
      "end_seconds": 262.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning. I live with my elderly mother. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.91,
      "end_seconds": 265.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.25,
      "end_seconds": 271.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, maybe, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.85,
      "end_seconds": 276.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.67,
      "end_seconds": 283.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Mm, not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.71,
      "end_seconds": 291.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with a peripheral neuropathy, probably related to diabetes at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.46,
      "end_seconds": 297.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Uh, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.65,
      "end_seconds": 308.26,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a peripheral neuropathy, probably related to diabetes is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.0,
      "end_seconds": 346.34,
      "duration_seconds": 30.34,
      "text": "We should do a B12 level for neuropathy. I'm going to put you on amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, long term. That should help with nerve pain. Check both feet daily and wear well-fitting shoes. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. I'd like you back in four weeks. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.16,
      "end_seconds": 352.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Great, um, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}